{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.QPlancherelSubNormalization","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.QPlancherelSubNormalization","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QPlancherelSubNormalization.Z3_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QPlancherelSubNormalization.Z3_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QPlancherelSubNormalization.lean#L113-L116","doc":"**Classical normalization at `n = 3`.** `Z₃(1) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QPlancherelSubNormalization.Z3_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QPlancherelSubNormalization.Z3_eq","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QPlancherelSubNormalization.lean#L98-L111","doc":"**Rationality at `n = 3`.**\n`Z₃(q) = q(q⁴+4q²+1) / ((q²+1)(q⁴+q²+1))` — again a rational function of `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QPlancherelSubNormalization.Z2_sub_normalized","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QPlancherelSubNormalization.Z2_sub_normalized","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QPlancherelSubNormalization.lean#L81-L96","doc":"**Sub-normalization / completeness defect at `n = 2`.** For every real\n`q > 0` with `q ≠ 1`, `Z₂(q) < 1`: the total q-Plancherel mass is strictly\nbelow 1, so `W_λ` is not a unitary vacuum-row probability measure at `q ≠ 1`.\nThe obstruction is exactly `0 < (q−1)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QPlancherelSubNormalization.Z2_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QPlancherelSubNormalization.Z2_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QPlancherelSubNormalization.lean#L76-L79","doc":"**Classical normalization.** `Z₂(1) = 1` (Plancherel at `q = 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QPlancherelSubNormalization.Z2_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QPlancherelSubNormalization.Z2_eq","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QPlancherelSubNormalization.lean#L65-L74","doc":"**Rationality at `n = 2`.** `Z₂(q) = 2q/(q²+1)` — a rational function of `q`,\nso the normalization's fibre→archimedean continuation is trivial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QPlancherelSubNormalization.Z3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QPlancherelSubNormalization.Z3","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QPlancherelSubNormalization.lean#L60-L63","doc":"**q-Plancherel partition function at `n = 3`.**\n`Z₃(q) = (d_q(3)² + d_q(2,1)² + d_q(1,1,1)²)/[3]_q!\n       = (1 + [2]_q² + 1)/([3]_q[2]_q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QPlancherelSubNormalization.Z2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QPlancherelSubNormalization.Z2","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QPlancherelSubNormalization.lean#L56-L58","doc":"**q-Plancherel partition function at `n = 2`.**\n`Z₂(q) = (d_q(2)² + d_q(1,1)²)/[2]_q! = (1 + 1)/[2]_q = 2/[2]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QPlancherelSubNormalization.bracket3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QPlancherelSubNormalization.bracket3","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QPlancherelSubNormalization.lean#L53-L54","doc":"The balanced quantum integer `[3]_q = q² + 1 + q⁻²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QPlancherelSubNormalization.bracket2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QPlancherelSubNormalization.bracket2","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QPlancherelSubNormalization.lean#L50-L51","doc":"The balanced quantum integer `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}